Distance formula: $d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$

Using the given endpoints $(2, -2)$ and $(10, 4)$, we can plug these values into the distance formula:

\begin{aligned}
d &= \sqrt{(10 - 2)^2 + (4 - (-2))^2} \\
&= \sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} \\
&= \sqrt{104} \\
&= 2\sqrt{26}
\end{aligned}

Therefore, the length of the line segment is $2\sqrt{26}$.
